@Begin

Metadata:
- Patient: Dorothy
- Age: 68
- Diagnosis: Early-stage Alzheimer's disease
- Language profile: Earlier stage, mostly fluent but occasional word-finding difficulty

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Good morning, Dorothy. Welcome to our office. How are you feeling today? *PAT* 

Dorothy: (..) I'm fine, thank you. I was just coming from... uh, Willow Creek. *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Willow Creek? That's a lovely place. Did you have a chance to enjoy the gardens while you were there? *PAT*

Dorothy: (pauses) Yes... the flowers. They were... (pauses again) lovely. *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* I'm glad you appreciated the beauty of nature. How have you been feeling lately? Any changes that concern you? *PAT*

Dorothy: (hesitates) A little... forgetful. I'll forget where I put... (trails off) thingamajig... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* It sounds like you might be having some trouble remembering things. Can you tell me what's been on your mind lately? Anything that's been causing you distress? *PAT*

Dorothy: (pauses) Nothing... just... (pauses again) oh, I was going to ask you... what's for... uh, lunch? *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* We'll be having a light lunch, Dorothy. I'll make sure to bring you something that's easy to eat. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities? *PAT*

Dorothy: (hesitates) Some... not as much. I've been having trouble... (struggles to find the word) what's the word... you know, when you can't... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* I think you might be thinking of "getting out the door." It can be frustrating when we struggle with daily tasks. Can you tell me more about what's been challenging for you? *PAT*

Dorothy: (pauses) It's just... I'll be doing... uh, laundry... and I'll forget where I put... (trails off) the... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* It sounds like you're having trouble with sequencing and organization. We can work on strategies to help you stay on track. Have you noticed any changes in your mood or behavior recently? *PAT*

Dorothy: (pauses) A little... anxious. I'll get... uh, upset... (pauses again) when I... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* It's understandable that you'd feel anxious when you're struggling with memory and daily tasks. We can work on some relaxation techniques to help you manage your emotions. Can you tell me about your family and friends? *PAT*

Dorothy: (pauses) Oh... they're... (pauses again) dear. I have... uh, children... and... (trails off) grandchildren... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* It's wonderful that you have a strong support system. We can work on some strategies to help you stay connected with your loved ones. Is there anything you'd like to ask me or discuss today? *PAT*

Dorothy: (pauses) No... I think that's all... (pauses again) for now... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Well, thank you for sharing with me today, Dorothy. We'll be in touch soon to discuss our next steps. *PAT*

Dorothy: (nods) Okay... thank you... *PAT*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* You're welcome, Dorothy. *PAT*

@End
